			(property "Description" "Qorvo DW3210 -- IEEE802.15.4z UWB transceiver IC, QFN40 5x5mm, non-PDoA variant. Pin names/numbers transcribed from the real Qorvo DW3000 Datasheet v1.3, Table 2 'DW3000 QFN & WLCSP Pin functions'. IMPORTANT: that table must be extracted with 'pdftotext -raw' -- the -layout mode mangles it (it renders VDD1 as pin 24 'Ground return for VDD2', which is wrong). Supplies: VDD1 pin 29 is the main supply (1.62-3.6V) and also feeds WAKEUP/EXTON/RSTn/SPI I/O; VDD2a pin 28 and VDD2b pin 23 are 2.4-3.6V (the datasheet notes ball F-15 needs ferrite isolation from B-15); VDD3 pin 26 is 1.5-3.6V. VTX_D pin 27 and VIO_D pin 38 are decoupling pins, each needing an external capacitor to ground -- they are NOT supply inputs and are typed passive here. Grounds: 10/11/12/14/15/16/17/19/20 are RF ground, 24 VSS2, 25 VSS3, 30 VSS1, 39/40 VSS digital. RF1 pin 18 needs a series 2pF cap; RF2 pin 13 is unused on this non-PDoA variant and must be terminated into 50 ohm through a 50 ohm trace. XTI pin 21 is the external-reference overdrive input used by this design's shared clock; XTO pin 22 then needs 1pF to ground. Symbol layout: pins 1-20 down the left, 21-40 down the right, numeric order."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
					(hide yes)
				)
			)
